      "notes": "Alone at Sea is a realistic survival game about the lone survivor of a shipwreck, adrift in a lifeboat. The rest of the crew is lost when the ship sinks in the opening scene. Your character can die in many ways, among them shark attacks (with blood in the water), drowning, hypothermia, thirst, starvation, disease, heatstroke and fire, and death is permanent. To eat, you catch, kill and butcher fish, sharks and seabirds. The game is frank about the body: relieving yourself over the side (no nudity), vomiting, dysentery, fever and hallucinations. The mood is bleak and isolating, with moments of horror. Night storms have bright lightning flashes. There is no sexual content, no nudity and no drug or alcohol use."
